hw - the parts of the machine the firmware can switch

  hw                     what this machine can switch, and how each stands
  hw wireless            just that one
  hw wireless on         switch it on
  hw camera off          switch it off

The parts, whichever of them a machine has: wireless, camera,
card_reader, usb_ports, modem. Only the ones this machine can switch
are listed, because a part it cannot switch is one it may not have.

A netbook of this age powers parts of itself down to save a battery, and
a part that is off is on no bus at all: it will not appear in `devices`
or `usb`, because there is nothing there to appear. That looks exactly
like hardware that is broken, and this is what tells the two apart.

The wireless key is wired to do the same for the radio, Fn+F2 on this
machine, and more besides: the network service takes the interface down
before the power goes and brings it back up after, in that order. No
press reaches it, for the reason `man hotkeys` gives. `hw` switches the
power alone, which is how it is asked for meanwhile and what serves the
parts no service speaks for.

On this machine the internal ports carry the camera and the card reader,
so switching usb_ports off takes both off the bus with it.
